/-- Claim B.3 in the explicit endpoint/bracket form.

This is the terminal no-bump/no-cross proof after hill elimination, with the
two endpoint facts that are external to the row-only auxiliary no-chord
invariant stated directly: terminal traces end on the bottom active row, and
each extracted hill interval carries the two bracketing strip atoms.  The
proof itself is self-contained from these data: non-convexity gives a finite
hill valley, no-hill gives a blocker, the maximal blocker block is internal,
the Claim B.2 strip barrier rules out lower-side entry, and finite ascent is
impossible. -/
theorem claimB3_connectedIntersections_of_atomized_endpoint_brackets
    {R : IndexedAuxiliaryPrefix L h} {hpos : 0 < h}
    {Q : PerfectPathPacking G R.X R.Y}
    {Q0 : TypeOneQStarFamily R hpos Q}
    {I : IterationInput R hpos Q0}
    {inv : TypeOneIterationInvariants I}
    (terminal_noBumpNoCross : NoBumpNoCross I)
    (terminal_aux_noChord : TerminalRowsAuxNoChord I inv)
    (no_hill : ClaimB3NoHill I inv)
    (atomized_trace : ClaimB3AtomizedTraceCompressionExtractionCertificate I inv)
    (trace_last_zero :
      ∀ j : Fin h,
        ((atomized_trace.blocks j).blockRow
          ⟨(atomized_trace.blocks j).len, by omega⟩).1 = 0)
    (hill_bracket :
      ∀ C : ClaimB3HillCandidateData I inv,
        Nonempty (ClaimB3HillBracketAtomData inv C)) :
    ClaimB3ConnectedIntersections I inv :=
  claimB3_connectedIntersections_of_endpointBracketTerminalProofData
    {
      terminal_noBumpNoCross := terminal_noBumpNoCross
      terminal_aux_noChord := terminal_aux_noChord
      no_hill := no_hill
      atomized_trace := atomized_trace
      trace_last_zero := trace_last_zero
      hill_bracket := hill_bracket
    }

/-- Claim B.3 in the trace-valley bracketing form.

This is the refined terminal no-bump/no-cross proof after hill elimination:
bracketing atoms are required only for hill candidates that are actually
extracted as valleys of the row-contact traces.  The successor step keeps the
blocker valley, obtains its own brackets, and then applies the same finite
ascent contradiction. -/
